  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":526547,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/230316152511-01-taylor-swift-0205-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-526547\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Getty Images </figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Recently, at the Taylor Swift concert held at the AT&amp;T Stadium in Arlington, Texas, an unusual incident occurred when a fan fell asleep during the show. It was a surprising moment, as the concert was a high-energy event that had fans jumping and screaming with excitement. The incident caught the attention of many attendees who were amazed to see someone sleeping while the performance was in full swing.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Several rumors and speculations emerged about why the fan might have fallen asleep. Some suggested that they were exhausted from a long day, while others assumed that they might have been under the influence of drugs or alcohol. However, the reason behind the fan's sleep remains a mystery. Despite this, the incident has become a topic of discussion and has generated humorous reactions on social media platforms. It goes to show that anything can happen at a live concert, and fans should be prepared for unexpected moments.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Swift during her three-day stint in Arlington, she also set a new record with 210,607 that came to see her, to <a href=\"https://www.fox4news.com/news/taylor-swift-fans-set-attendance-record-at-att-stadium\">Fox 4 in Dallas</a>. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Also according to The Dallas Morning News, Swift also gift a lucky fan a 22 hat during her 'Eras  Tour.'</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cqft08BusDY/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link\",\"type\